const body = "<h1>Getting started</h1>\n<p>howl-go renders the same templ components on the server, into static files, and inside the browser via WebAssembly. One Go module, no Node, no npm, no client framework.</p>\n<h2>Install</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">go mod init example.com/myapp\ngo get github.com/mirairoad/howl-go@v0.1.0\ngo get -tool github.com/a-h/templ/cmd/templ@v0.3.1020\n</code></pre>\n<p>The tool command matters: a dependency's <code>tool</code> directives do not propagate\ninto the consuming module.</p>\n<h2>The smallest app</h2>\n<p>Three files: a document shell, a page, and a <code>main.go</code>.</p>\n<pre><code>client/pages/app.templ     the document shell — reserved, never a route\nclient/pages/index.templ   /\nmain.go\n</code></pre>\n<p><code>client/pages/index.templ</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-templ\">package pages\n\ntempl Page() {\n\t&lt;h1&gt;Hello&lt;/h1&gt;\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p><code>main.go</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-go\">a := app.New(app.Config{\n\tRoutes: pages.FsClientRoutes(),\n\tShell:  pages.App,\n\tPublic: public,\n})\nlog.Fatal(a.Listen(a.Mux()))\n</code></pre>\n<p><code>FsClientRoutes()</code> is generated by walking the page directory — you never register a route by hand.</p>\n<h2>Build</h2>\n<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">go run github.com/mirairoad/howl-go/core/cmd/fsroutes@v0.1.0 -module your.module/client/pages\ngo tool templ generate\ngo build .\n</code></pre>\n<p>The example apps wrap this in a <code>Makefile</code>; <code>make</code> runs all three steps.</p>\n<h2>What you get</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>first paint</td>\n<td>server-rendered HTML, crawlable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>navigation</td>\n<td>client-side, prefetched on intent</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>a route marked <code>.client</code></td>\n<td>rendered in the browser, zero bytes over the wire</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>make static</code></td>\n<td>every static route written to disk</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"
